          %h2#references References
          %p In the traditional physicist’s string theory introductions one finds Chan-Paton bundles discussed for instance
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clifford+Johnson"}> Clifford Johnson
                , section 2.4 of
                %em D-Brane primer
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0007170"}> arXiv:hep-th/0007170
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Tong"}> David Tong
                , around p. 66 of:
                %em Lectures on String Theory
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0908.0333"}> arxiv:0908.0333
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.damtp.cam.ac.uk/user/tong/string.html"} webpage
          %p
            These lectures tend to ignore most of the global subtleties though. For traditional discussion of the
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Freed-Witten-Kapustin+anomaly"} Freed-Witten-Kapustin anomaly
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/higher+geometry"} higher geometry
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+prequantum+field+theory"} extended prequantum field theory
            is due to section 5.4 of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Domenico+Fiorenza"}> Domenico Fiorenza
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hisham+Sati"} Hisham Sati
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"} Urs Schreiber
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/A+higher+stacky+perspective+on+Chern-Simons+theory"} A higher stacky perspective on Chern-Simons theory
              \.
          %p Lecture notes along these lines are at
          %ul
            %li
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometry+of+physics"} geometry of physics
          %p
            Discussion of the derivation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+theory"} Yang-Mills theory
            on the D-brane from open
            = succeed "/" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+scattering+amplitudes"} string scattering amplitudes
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/string+field+theory"} string field theory
            includes
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/David+Gross"}> David Gross
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Superstring modifications of Einstein’s equations
              %strong 277
              (1986) 1-10. &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/0550-3213(86)90429-3"}> doi:10.1016/0550-3213(86)90429-3
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p and for the non-abelian case:
          %ul
            %li
              Semyon Klevtsov,
              %em Yang-Mills theory from String field theory on D-branes
              (
              %a{:href => "http://www.mi.uni-koeln.de/~klevtsov/cargese02.pdf"}> pdf
              )
